  "body": "Final production-readiness stage, stacked on PR #57.\n\nThis tranche does not add another semantic interpretation layer. It turns the accumulated SCAN work into a commit- and byte-specific release certification process.\n\nAdds:\n- SCAN engine version 1.0.0 candidate;\n- stronger packaged qualification requiring the current coverage/gap, uncertainty, triage, and layered-provenance projections;\n- expanded LLM credential stripping during mechanical qualification;\n- `scan-body release-certify` local exact-package certification;\n- `scan-body verify-release-certification`;\n- sealed local certification manifest with package-manifest and qualification hashes;\n- explicit separation between local mechanical certification and CI-only release evidence;\n- final certification contract documentation;\n- Linux/macOS/Windows matrix on Python 3.11/3.12/3.13;\n- complete inherited regression suite;\n- live Linux network-denied authorized-runtime validation;\n- wrong-plan-hash fail-closed proof;\n- clean wheel build/install and installed-CLI scan smoke;\n- deterministic source archive;\n- aggregate `V1_CI_RELEASE_CERTIFICATE.json` and `V1_CI_MANIFEST.json` emitted only after all prerequisite gates succeed.\n\nAuthority boundaries remain explicit:\n- ordinary SCAN stays static/non-executing;\n- runtime evidence remains explicitly authorized and sidecar-only;\n- local package PASS is not allowed to self-promote into CI-wide certification;\n- certification applies only to the exact commit/package bytes tested;\n- no universal semantic completeness, runtime equivalence, hostile-code sandbox, distributed locking, exhaustive fuzzing, or production SLA is implied.\n\nThis is the final stage in:\ncoverage/gaps \u2192 uncertainty challenger \u2192 triage ranking \u2192 layered provenance \u2192 parity scenarios/distribution \u2192 broader calibration \u2192 independent reconstruction proof \u2192 authorized runtime validation \u2192 operational hardening \u2192 v1.0 certification.",
